— the onboarding\nchain starts at license validation and Konflux onboarding. Fork readiness (including whether the\nkagenti-extensions fork actually exists and is synced) is verified by the upstream validation\nInvestigation (E001); if a fork is missing, repo-onboarding work is added as remediation.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality, CRD stability, and midstream fork readiness | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Resolve Keycloak runtime dependency and ClientRegistrationController TP configuration | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Decide TP dashboard integration depth (project tab vs standalone navigation) | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component removal | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Resolve OTEL trace sink requirement from parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | Konflux onboarding: kagenti-operator image (FIPS Go build, UBI9) | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | Konflux onboarding: AuthBridge proxy sidecar image (FIPS Go build, UBI9) | Implementation | Kagenti | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | License validation for kagenti midstream repositories | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries for disconnected install | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | Dashboard BFF plugin, feature flag, and agent list view | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | QE test plan and E2E validation for kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P0 |\n| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Installation, upgrade, and agent image contract documentation | Implementation | Docs | P0 |\n\nMain-plan epics: 14. Critical path length: 5\n(E001 → E010 → E011 → E013 → E014).\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001 --> E010\n    E003 --> E010\n    E005 --> E010\n    E010 --> E011\n    E010 --> E012\n    E004 --> E012\n    E010 --> E013\n    E011 --> E013\n    E001 --> E014\n    E003 --> E014\n    E007 --> E014\n    E008 --> E014\n    E009 --> E014\n    E010 --> E014\n    E011 --> E014\n    E012 --> E014\n    E013 --> E014\n```\n\nRoots (no dependencies): E001, E002, E003, E004, E005, E006, E007, E008, E009.\n\nBranch epics (not main-plan nodes, excluded from the diagram and critical path):\n\n- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E015` — AuthBridge envoy + lite variant Konflux components\n  (gated by E002, outcome B: all three variants needed for TP).\n- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E016` — OTEL trace sink integration for agent telemetry\n  (gated by E006, outcome B: OTEL trace sink confirmed as a TP requirement).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| E001 → E010 | Rule 3 | Upstream functional gaps or CRD instability change which controllers/manifests the component controller pins and deploys (rewrite gate) |\n| E003 → E010 | Rule 3 | Whether ClientRegistrationController is enabled for TP (Keycloak dependency) changes the manifest overlays and deployed configuration |\n| E005 → E010 | Rule 3 | Cross-namespace CRD/CR cleanup semantics change the garbage-collection logic the controller must implement |\n| E010 → E011 | Rule 13 | The CSV declares the KagentiOperator component CRD and RBAC produced by the controller work — build-against artifact |\n| E010 → E012 | Rule 13 | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the DSC kagenti component state — the dashboard builds against the component CR/schema created by the controller work |\n| E004 → E012 | Rule 3 | Tab-in-project-view vs standalone navigation rewrites the dashboard BFF/UI scope (~1 vs ~2 sprints) |\n| E010 → E013 | Rule 12 | Component-lifecycle E2E tests build against the controller's Managed/Removed behavior |\n| E011 → E013 | Rule 12 | Disconnected-install validation exercises the CSV RELATED_IMAGE entries |\n| E001 → E014 | Rule 3 / 11 | Docs must describe a validated image contract and stable CRD; docs are last |\n| E003 → E014 | Rule 3 | Keycloak external-dependency documentation content depends on the resolution |\n| E007 → E014 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics |\n| E008 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n| E009 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n| E010 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n| E011 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n| E012 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n| E013 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n\nDeliberate **non-edges** (Rule 10 / Rule 13 configuration-reference exception):\n\n- No edge from the Konflux onboarding epics (E007, E008) to the component controller (E010),\n  CSV packaging (E011), or QE (E013). The Konflux-built image digests are configuration\n  references filled in at execution time; the coupling is enforced by acceptance criteria\n  (\"Konflux-built image with SHA256-pinned digest available\") on the consuming epics, never by\n  DAG dependencies. Wiring such edges would serialize work that must run in parallel.\n- No edge between license validation (E009) and Konflux onboarding (E007/E008) — Rule 7/8:\n  parallel start. Rule 9 (license → general implementation serial) has no target here: this\n  strategy contains no general-purpose implementation epic built on the kagenti code (runtime\n  features are out of scope, tracked in RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589). A license failure would\n  remediate dependency sets inside the Konflux/Dockerfile work, not change epic structure.\n- No repo-onboarding epic: midstream forks already exist per the strategy dependency table.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E007 |\n| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern | P0 | E010 |\n| `managementState: Removed` cleans up all operator-managed resources | P0 | E010 (semantics informed by E005) |\n| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E007, E008, E009 (process constraint on all Kagenti midstream work) |\n| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E010 |\n| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin + feature flag | P1 | E012 |\n| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected install | P1 | E011 |\n| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E008 |\n| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if free) | P2 | E007, E008 (build-configuration acceptance criteria, not separate epics — incidental to the same build work) |\n\nAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements; no epic without HLR (or strategy-AC) trace.\n\nStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage notes:\n\n- DSC enablement, Removed cleanup, documentation MUSTs → E010, E005, E014.\n- Console/API discovery of agents → E012 (TP read-only agent list).\n- AgentRuntime CR selection/discovery, metadata sync on rollouts, degraded condition (SHOULD),\n  Deployment-deletion garbage collection → upstream operator runtime behavior, explicitly out of\n  scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588). Not covered by design.\n- Sandbox auto-registration (COULD) → out of scope; see Health Warnings.\n- OTEL trace sink (open MUST from parent RFE) → E006 + BRANCH-B-E016.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Open parent-RFE MUST (OTEL trace sink)** — the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries an OTEL\n   trace sink MUST not reflected in this strategy's HLRs; under team discussion. Modeled as\n   Investigation E006 with conditional branch epic BRANCH-B-E016. If the discussion lands late,\n  