teria\n\n- Gap-analysis document published, enumerating per-controller functional status, CRD stability\n  assessment, and fork readiness for both kagenti repositories, with a clear L-vs-XL effort\n  verdict and any proposed TP scope reductions.\n- A pinned upstream/midstream commit or tag is identified as the productization baseline for\n  manifests and builds.\n- If a midstream fork is missing or materially out of sync, the remediation (fork creation or\n  sync backport) is identified and sized.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Supports P0 HLRs (Konflux-built operator images, DSC component enablement) by validating the\n  code base they productize; the effort estimate and possibly the manifest scope of the platform\n  integration depend on this investigation's outcome.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59850,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e9b625983a557d","agent_id":"a91ca77782a9ba1e7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"d0a2d027-a216-4abb-99fc-2c2acacfbd51","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:17:40.725Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
