{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-d40254d3-0740-421c-8932-2c8166c033f5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e5cc72ed5ac6e95","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b6wumj_a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E003.md","content":"# Resolve Keycloak runtime dependency and ClientRegistrationController TP configuration\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation determines whether the kagenti-operator requires Keycloak as a runtime\ndependency. The operator's ClientRegistrationController manages OAuth2 client registration with\nKeycloak; if Keycloak is required, it becomes an external dependency that must be documented and\nvalidated (Keycloak deployment itself is out of scope and managed outside this strategy). The\ninvestigation also determines whether the ClientRegistrationController can be disabled for Tech\nPreview, which changes the manifest overlays and deployed configuration of the productized\ncomponent.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Inspect the upstream kagenti-operator to determine whether the ClientRegistrationController\n  (and any other controller) hard-requires a Keycloak instance at runtime, and under what\n  configuration.\n- Determine whether the ClientRegistrationController can be disabled or left dormant for Tech\n  Preview without affecting AgentRuntime reconciliation or AuthBridge sidecar injection.\n- Decide the TP configuration: controller enabled (Keycloak documented as an external\n  prerequisite) or disabled (deferred to a later release).\n- Record what must be documented for customers about Keycloak as an external dependency.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Documented determination of the Keycloak runtime dependency, with the upstream code paths that\n  establish it.\n- TP configuration decision recorded (ClientRegistrationController enabled/disabled) with the\n  corresponding manifest overlay settings to apply.\n- If Keycloak is required, the documentation requirements (external prerequisite description,\n  validation steps) are handed off to the documentation workstream.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Qualifies the P0 HLRs for DSC component enablement and Tech Preview opt-in: the answer changes\n  what the component controller deploys (manifest overlays) and what the documentation covers.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":61082,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e9b625983a557d","agent_id":"a91ca77782a9ba1e7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"114a7f8f-8081-46d6-95c8-882d36422219","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:17:56.049Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
