{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ed424675-daed-4b21-80ff-6a07019d52c4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bf4962e21cb9f259","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b6wumj_a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E005.md","content":"# Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component removal\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves what happens to user-created AgentRuntime CRs when the kagenti\ncomponent is disabled via the DataScienceCluster. The component controller cleans up\noperator-managed resources in `redhat-ods-applications`, but user-created AgentRuntime CRs in\nother namespaces may become orphaned. The Platform / ODH Operator team must decide whether\ncomponent removal includes cross-namespace CRD deletion (which destroys user-created CRs) or\nleaves them orphaned, and document the chosen semantics so the controller's garbage-collection\nlogic implements a defined behavior.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Decide the removal semantics: delete the AgentRuntime CRD cluster-wide (removing user CRs in\n  all namespaces) versus leaving user-created CRs in place on component removal.\n- Evaluate how existing platform component controllers handle analogous cases and whether a\n  finalizer-based enumeration of owned resources is needed.\n- Record the decision and the concrete cleanup contract (resource list, namespace scope,\n  ordering) the component controller must implement.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Decision recorded with rationale, covering: controller Deployment, RBAC (ClusterRoles,\n  ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings), the AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook\n  configuration, namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications`, and user-created\n  AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces.\n- The cleanup contract is specified precisely enough to implement and to test in E2E (resources\n  in multiple namespaces).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Qualifies the P0 HLR \"When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed\n  resources are cleaned up\": the answer defines what \"all\" means for cross-namespace user\n  resources and changes the controller's garbage-collection scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":62064,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e9b625983a557d","agent_id":"a91ca77782a9ba1e7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"1c224a03-b6ff-42dc-a00b-35144359be7f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:10.514Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
