 namespace (`redhat-ods-applications`), image references, and RBAC adjustments.\n- Implement `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` deploys the operator (Deployment, CRDs,\n  RBAC, mutating webhook); `Removed` deletes all operator-managed resources — controller\n  Deployment, ClusterRoles/ClusterRoleBindings/Roles/RoleBindings, the AgentRuntime CRD, the\n  mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications` —\n  per the decided cleanup semantics (including the cross-namespace CR handling decision).\n- Default the component to `Removed` (explicit opt-in) for Tech Preview.\n- Apply the decided TP configuration for the ClientRegistrationController / Keycloak dependency\n  in the manifest overlays.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti component `managementState: Managed`, when\n  the DSC controller reconciles, the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in\n  `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image (SHA256-pinned digest available as a\n  configuration reference), measured by a Ready deployment with `app=kagenti-operator`.\n- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller reconciles, all\n  operator-managed resources are deleted per the decided cleanup contract (verified for\n  resources in multiple namespaces), measured by no remaining Deployment and the AgentRuntime\n  CRD returning not found.\n- Component defaults to `Removed` (opt-in); existing clusters are unaffected by upgrade.\n- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n- Manifests are pinned to the validated upstream/midstream baseline commit.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component\n  controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed`.\n- P0: When disabled, all operator-managed resources are cleaned up (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs,\n  namespace-scoped resources).\n- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64471,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81e9b625983a557d","agent_id":"a91ca77782a9ba1e7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"395f76d6-2bd2-4f24-86c1-40d8595cb06d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:18:54.082Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8006"}
