{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-87ee477578d53299","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 14\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy triage: **not below threshold** (L effort, 4 affected code components, 5 involved teams,\n13\tmultiple architecturally distinct work streams) and **not docs-only** (three of four affected\n14\tcomponents require code changes). Full decomposition follows.\n15\t\n16\tStaff Engineer / SME Input section is empty (template placeholder only) — no overrides to log.\n17\t\n18\t## Component Name Mappings\n19\t\n20\tCanonical RHAI Jira components (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) assigned to epics:\n21\t\n22\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n23\t| --- | --- | --- |\n24\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | New component; no architecture-context file exists (not yet in platform) |\n25\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | New component; no architecture-context file exists |\n26\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Existing platform root operator (architecture context: rhods-operator.md) |\n27\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Existing console (architecture context: odh-dashboard.md) |\n28\t| Docs workstream | Documentation | |\n29\t| QE workstream | QE | |\n30\t| OTEL trace sink question | Model and Agent Observability | |\n31\t\n32\tNew-component detection: neither kagenti-operator nor kagenti-extensions has an architecture\n33\tcontext file, so both get the new-component onboarding treatment (Rule 20). However, the\n34\tstrategy's dependency table states the midstream forks already exist\n35\t(`opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` — status \"Exists\"; `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` is\n36\tnamed as the build source