E012 | Dashboard BFF plugin, feature flag, and agent list view | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | QE test plan and E2E validation for kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P0 |\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Installation, upgrade, and agent image contract documentation | Implementation | Docs | P0 |\n59\t\n60\tMain-plan epics: 14. Critical path length: 5\n61\t(E001 → E010 → E011 → E013 → E014).\n62\t\n63\t## Dependency DAG\n64\t\n65\t```mermaid\n66\tgraph TD\n67\t    E001 --> E010\n68\t    E003 --> E010\n69\t    E005 --> E010\n70\t    E010 --> E011\n71\t    E010 --> E012\n72\t    E004 --> E012\n73\t    E010 --> E013\n74\t    E011 --> E013\n75\t    E001 --> E014\n76\t    E003 --> E014\n77\t    E007 --> E014\n78\t    E008 --> E014\n79\t    E009 --> E014\n80\t    E010 --> E014\n81\t    E011 --> E014\n82\t    E012 --> E014\n83\t    E013 --> E014\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\tRoots (no dependencies): E001, E002, E003, E004, E005, E006, E007, E008, E009.\n87\t\n88\tBranch epics (not main-plan nodes, excluded from the diagram and critical path):\n89\t\n90\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E015` — AuthBridge envoy + lite variant Konflux components\n91\t  (gated by E002, outcome B: all three variants needed for TP).\n92\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E016` — OTEL trace sink integration for agent telemetry\n93\t  (gated by E006, outcome B: OTEL trace sink confirmed as a TP requirement).\n94\t\n95\t## DAG Justification\n96\t\n97\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n98\t| --- | --- | --- |\n99\t| E001 → E010 | Rule 3 | Upstream functional gaps or CRD instability change which controllers/manifests the component controller pins and deploys (rewrite gate) |\n100\t| E003 → E010 | Rule 3 | Whether ClientRegistrationController is enabled for TP (Keycloak dependency) changes the manifest overlays and deployed configuration |\n101\t| E005 → E010 | Rule 3 | Cross-namespace CRD/CR cleanup semantics change the garbage-collection logic the controller must implement |\n102\t| E010 → E011 | Rule 13 | The CSV declares the KagentiOperator component CRD and RBAC produced by the controller work — build-against artifact |\n103\t| E010 → E012 | Rule 13 | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the DSC kagenti component state — the dashboard builds against the component CR/schema created by the controller work |\n104\t| E004 → E012 | Rule 3 | Tab-in-project-view vs standalone navigation rewrites the dashboard BFF/UI scope (~1 vs ~2 sprints) |\n105\t| E010 → E013 | Rule 12 | Component-lifecycle E2E tests build against the controller's Managed/Removed behavior |\n106\t| E011 → E013 | Rule 12 | Disconnected-install validation exercises the CSV RELATED_IMAGE entries |\n107\t| E001 → E014 | Rule 3 / 11 | Docs must describe a validated image contract and stable CRD; docs are last |\n108\t| E003 → E014 | Rule 3 | Keycloak external-dependency documentation content depends on the resolution |\n109\t| E007 → E014 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics |\n110\t| E008 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n111\t| E009 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n112\t| E010 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n113\t| E011 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n114\t| E012 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n115\t| E013 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n116\t\n117\tDeliberate **non-edges** (Rule 10 / Rule 13 configuration-reference exception):\n118\t\n119\t- No edge from the Konflux onboarding epics (E007, E008) to the component controller (E010),\n120\t  CSV packaging (E011), or QE (E013). The Konflux-built image digests are configuration\n121\t  references filled in at execution time; the coupling is enforced by acceptance criteria\n122\t  (\"Konflux-built image with SHA256-pinned digest available\") on the consuming epics, never by\n123\t  DAG dependencies. Wiring such edges would serialize work that must run in parallel.\n124\t- No edge between license validation (E009) and Konflux onboarding (E007/E008) — Rule 7/8:\n125\t  parallel start. Rule 9 (license → general implementation serial) has no target here: this\n126\t  strategy contains no general-purpose implementation epic built on the kagenti code (runtime\n127\t  features are out of scope, tracked in RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589). A license failure would\n128\t  remediate dependency sets inside the Konflux/Dockerfile work, not change epic structure.\n129\t- No repo-onboarding epic: midstream forks already exist per the strategy dependency table.\n130\t\n131\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n132\t\n133\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n134\t| --- | --- | --- |\n135\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E007 |\n136\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern | P0 | E010 |\n137\t| `managementState: Removed` cleans up all operator-managed resources | P0 | E010 (semantics informed by E005) |\n138\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E007, E008, E009 (process constraint on all Kagenti midstream work) |\n139\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E010 |\n140\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin + feature flag | P1 | E012 |\n141\t| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected install | P1 | E011 |\n142\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E008 |\n143\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if free) | P2 | E007, E008 (build-configuration acceptance criteria, not separate epics — incidental to the same build work) |\n144\t\n145\tAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements; no epic without HLR (or strategy-AC) trace.\n146\t\n147\tStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage notes:\n148\t\n149\t- DSC enablement, Removed cleanup, documentation MUSTs → E010, E005, E014.\n150\t- Console/API discovery of agents → E012 (TP read-only agent list).\n151\t- AgentRuntime CR selection/discovery, metadata sync on rollouts, degraded condition (SHOULD),\n152\t  Deployment-deletion garbage collection → upstream operator runtime behavior, explicitly out of\n153\t  scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588). Not covered by design.\n154\t- Sandbox auto-registration (COULD) → out of scope; see Health Warnings.\n155\t- OTEL trace sink (open MUST from parent RFE) → E006 + BRANCH-B-E016.\n156\t\n157\t## Health Warnings\n158\t\n159\t1. **Open parent-RFE MUST (OTEL trace sink)** — the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries an OTEL\n160\t   trace sink MUST not reflected in this strategy's HLRs; under team discussion. Modeled as\n161\t   Investigation E006 with conditional branch epic BRANCH-B-E016. If the discussion lands late,\n162\t   TP docs and QE scope shift.\n163\t2. **Dashboard architecture-context discrepancy** — architecture context (odh-dashboard.md,\n164\t   RHOAI 3.6-ea.1) shows an existing `agent-ops` federated BFF module with per-agent RBAC that\n165\t   the strategy does not mention (it cites only 7 plugins / ports 8043-8643). The dashboard epic\n166\t   must reconcile reuse/extension of the existing agent-ops module against building a new kagenti\n167\t   plugin before committing to a new BFF container and port.\n168\t3. **COULD acceptance criterion (sandbox auto-registration) uncovered** — runtime behavior out of\n169\t   scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7589), and the OpenShell Sandbox CR interplay open question remains with\n170\t   the Kagenti team. Intentional gap; flagged so review does not treat it as an omission.\n171\t4. **Minimal image contract undecided (A2A vs simpler format)** — owned by RHAIRFE-7588; the\n172\t   documentation epic carries it as an acceptance criterion (contract finalized and documented),\n173\t   not an Investigation here, because no epic in this strategy changes existence/approach based\n174\t   on the answer.\n175\t5. **kagenti-extensions midstream fork existence assumed** — the strategy references\n176\t   `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` as the build source but only lists the operator fork as\n177\t   confirmed. Verified by E001; if missing, repo-onboarding is added (add_remediation).\n178\t6. **Konflux pipeline capacity (\"Needs submission\")** — lead-time risk on the critical path to\n179\t   the 3.5 release. The Konflux epics are DAG roots precisely so onboarding submission starts\n180\t   immediately, per the strategy's own risk mitigation.\n181\t7. **Docs epic (P0 via strategy priority Critical) is blocked by P1 dashboard and CSV epics** —\n182\t   intentional consequence of the docs-last rule (docs describe what was built); not a priority\n183\t   inversion to fix.\n184\t8. **Strategy data-quality note** — a proposed AC references CRD\n185\t   `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev` (apparent typo for `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`); worth\n186\t   correcting during PM/Engineering validation of the proposed ACs.\n187\t9. **No scope traps detected** — NFRs (FIPS, container security, disconnected install) map to\n188\t   acceptance criteria on the Konflux/packaging epics and do not imply nonexistent\n189\t   infrastructure; out-of-scope items are consistent with the NFRs.\n190\t\n191\t## Tiered Delivery\n192\t\n193\tNot applicable. The external dependencies (upstream kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions)\n194\talready exist and are functional per the dependency table; no dependency with uncertain timing\n195\tgates a user-facing deliverable. The only timing risk (Konflux capacity) is an internal lead-time\n196\titem mitigated by starting the onboarding epics as DAG roots.\n197\t\n198\t## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n199\t\n200\t**E002 — AuthBridge variant set for TP** (bounded, 2 outcomes):\n201\t\n202\t- Outcome A (proxy only for TP): main plan stands as-is; the AuthBridge proxy Konflux epic\n203\t  (E008) is the complete variant scope. No branch epic.\n204\t- Outcome B (envoy and/or lite also needed for 3.5): `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E015` adds the\n205\t  additional Konflux components (and corresponding CSV entries).\n206\t\n207\t**E006 — OTEL trace sink requirement** (bounded, 2 outcomes):\n208\t\n2