{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-906756776b6805e4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n3\ttitle: Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality, CRD stability, and midstream\n4\t  fork readiness\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n6\tcomponent: Agentic\n7\tteam: Kagenti\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality, CRD stability, and midstream fork readiness\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's critical sprint-1 assumption: that a functional\n31\tupstream kagenti-operator exists in the `kagenti` GitHub org with the AgentRuntime CRD and core\n32\tcontrollers, and that the midstream forks under `opendatahub-io` are set up and synced. The\n33\tdeliverable is a gap-analysis document that determines whether the productization effort holds\n34\tat L or must be renegotiated, and which upstream manifests/commits the platform integration\n35\tshould pin.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Validate the upstream kagenti-operator against the controller inventory in architecture\n40\t  context overlay 0014: AgentRuntimeReconciler (including metadata fetch from\n41\t  `/.well-known/agent-card.json`), MLflowReconciler, and ClientRegistrationController.\n42\t- Confirm the AgentRuntime CRD (`agent.kagenti.dev/v1alpha1`) schema is stable enough for Tech\n43\t  Preview (field changes after productization require migration).\n44\t- Verify the midstream fork `opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` exists and is synced with upstream,\n45\t  and confirm whether `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` exists as a buildable fork; establish\n46\t  the fork sync process if not yet defined.\n47\t- Confirm the kagenti-operator can run in `redhat-ods-applications` alongside other platform\n48\t  operators without RBAC conflicts.\n49\t- Produce a gap-analysis document: if gaps exceed roughly 2 sprints of upstream work, propose a\n50\t  TP scope reduction (e.g., defer MLflowReconciler and/or ClientRegistrationController) for\n51\t  negotiation.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Gap-analysis document published, enumerating per-controller functional status, CRD stability\n56\t  assessment, and fork readiness for both kagenti repositories, with a clear L-vs-XL effort\n57\t  verdict and any proposed TP scope reductions.\n58\t- A pinned upstream/midstream commit or tag is identified as the productization baseline for\n59\t  manifests and builds.\n60\t- If a midstream fork is missing or materially out of sync, the remediation (fork creation or\n61\t  sync backport) is identified and sized.\n62\t\n63\t## HLR Traceability\n64\t\n65\t- Supports P0 HLRs (Konflux-built operator images, DSC component enablement) by validating the\n66\t  code base they productize; the effort estimate and possibly the manifest scope of the platform\n67\t  integration depend on this investigation's outcome.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7235745e7d45a0a","agent_id":"ac2507bfc800dc5e2","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"56b17122-18dc-45e2-b3fb-d6bacc2abce8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:23:33.935Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-906756776b6805e4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
