uite for the same component, and the underlying P1 HLR (CSV packaging) is\nindependently plannable via E011.\n\n### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n\nAll 17 edges in the mermaid diagram match the target epics' frontmatter `dependencies`\nexactly, and vice versa; arrows run dependency → dependent per convention. No cycles.\nCritical path E001 → E010 → E011 → E013 → E014 (length 5) is within the L-strategy heuristic\n(5-7). Rule 10 is fully respected: konflux-onboarding epics (E007, E008, BRANCH-B-E015)\nhave no edges to any general-implementation epic in either direction (E010, E011, E012,\nE013, BRANCH-B-E016 all checked); image digests are correctly handled as configuration\nreferences via Rule 25 build-pipeline-green ACs. Rule 7/8 respected (no license-validation →\nkonflux edges). Both branch files set `branch` and `gated_by` correctly, and no main-plan\nepic lists a branch epic in its dependencies. Non-edges (E001 ↛ E007/E008 parallel start)\nare explicitly justified by the strategy's own Konflux lead-time risk mitigation. Minor:\nbranch epics' dependency sets are thin relative to their content — E015's CSV modifications\nand E016's \"productized operator\" wiring implicitly build on main-plan epics (E011, E010)\nwith no noted relationship; acceptable for plan-document branch nodes but worth making\nexplicit.\n\n### 3. Epic Boundaries (0/2)\n\nMain-plan boundaries are clean: each epic is a single component/team tuple matching the\nstrategy's affected-components table; Konflux work is split per image family (E007/E008);\nCSV packaging is correctly separated from Konflux onboarding (E011, Platform team); no\nscope duplication between siblings. However, two major issues in the conditional-branch\nepics:\n\n- **Major — BRANCH-B-E015 spans two teams/components.** Its scope includes \"Add the\n  corresponding SHA256-pinned `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries to the ClusterServiceVersion\" —\n  that is rhods-operator CSV work, which the strategy's Impacted Teams table assigns to\n  Platform / ODH Operator and which the main plan itself places in E011 (AI Core Platform,\n  Platform team). Assigning it to a Kagenti-team/Agentic-component epic contradicts the\n  decomposition's own boundary logic (the main plan split exactly this Konflux-vs-CSV work\n  into E008 and E011). The CSV work should be a Platform-owned extension of E011 or a\n  separate branch epic owned by Platform.\n- **Major — BRANCH-B-E016 mixes work-product types.** It bundles code implementation\n  (OTEL trace sink wiring) with customer-facing content authoring (\"Document the trace sink\n  configuration for customers\" is a scope item and an acceptance criterion). These are\n  different kinds of work with different review criteria and should be separate even within\n  the branch (the main-plan docs-authoring epic E014 does not cover this content, since it\n  has no dependency on E006 or the branch).\n- Minor — E010's scope (CRD + controller + registry + kustomize manifests + lifecycle)\n  maps to the strategy's 2-3 sprint component-controller estimate, at or slightly above the\n  ~2-week epic guideline; defensible as one atomic pattern-following change, but it is the\n  largest epic in the set.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (1/2)\n\nAll six Investigations genuinely resolve uncertainty that changes downstream structure or\nexistence (E001 rewrite gate on E010; E002/E006 select branch epics; E003 changes E010\nmanifest overlays; E004 rewrites E012 scope; E005 changes E010 GC logic), and all\nImplementation epics produce concrete artifacts. All `gated_by` targets appear in their\nepics' direct `dependencies`, and every `gate_failure_impact` has both `action` and\n`fallback_approach` populated. One gating-metadata issue: **E010 lists three Investigations\nin `dependencies` (E001, E003, E005) but sets `gated_by` only on E001** — its own\ndescription says it is \"gated on three resolved unknowns,\" each of which changes its scope,\nso E003 and E005 are Investigation dependencies missing `gated_by`. Likewise **E014 lists\nE001 (Investigation) in `dependencies` without `gated_by`** (only E003 is marked). Since\n`gated_by` is single-valued in the schema, the secondary outcome-couplings should be\nmodeled as explicit AC gates (as done for image digests) or otherwise marked, so automated\nconsumers detect all real gates. Types and signal rubric fields are otherwise correct\n(`ai_signals` on Implementation, `investigation_signals` on Investigation).\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (2/2)\n\nEvery epic uses the type-appropriate signal field, and all 16 ai-signals files exist with\nfrontmatter values matching the rationale tables exactly. Investigation signals are\nconsistent with content: the three product-decision investigations (E002, E004, E006)\ncorrectly score `human_judgment_required: -2` / `source_accessibility: 0`, while the\nsource-readable investigations (E001, E003, E005) score `source_accessibility: 1`.\nImplementation signals are well-justified: E010/E012 correctly carry `open_questions: -1`\n(gated on investigations), E009 correctly scores `existing_foundation: 0` (new scan\ntargets), and BRANCH-B-E016's negative signals match the strategy's lack of technical\ndetail for the OTEL wiring. No contradictions between signal values, rationales, and\nstrategy content found. (Arithmetic/thresholds not checked, per instructions.)\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\n\nEvery epic has testable acceptance criteria, mostly in Given/when/then or measurably\nphrased form. Rule-mandated ACs are present on every applicable epic: all three\nkonflux-onboarding epics (E007, E008, BRANCH-B-E015) carry both `check-payload` FIPS and\ngreen-build/SHA256-digest ACs; E010 (rhods-operator changes) carries the build-pipeline-green\nAC; docs-authoring E014 carries the technical-review and docs-content-process ACs. No\nreplacement epics exist (new component), so the rollback/feature-flag rule does not apply.\nNo epic body references sibling epics by draft ID (grep verified — all E0xx occurrences are\nfrontmatter fields).\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nAll strategy scope is covered: Konflux onboarding (E007/E008 + branch E015), component\ncontroller (E010), CSV packaging (E011), dashboard integration (E012), QE (E013),\ndocumentation (E014). All five strategy open-questions table entries map to investigations\n(E001-E006), and the two top-level open questions are explicitly dispositioned (minimal\nimage contract → E014 AC with justification; Sandbox CR interplay → flagged intentional gap\nin Health Warnings, runtime scope). All seven proposed ACs and the top-level MUSTs are\neither covered (AC1/3/4/5/6/7 → E010/E007/E008/E012/E011/E013/E014) or explicitly justified\nas out of scope per the strategy's own Out-of-Scope section (runtime discovery/metadata/GC\nACs → RHAIRFE-7587/7588). All strategy risks are carried forward into epic scope (Konflux\nlead time → E007 scope; webhook ordering → E013 scope; port collision → E012 AC; orphaned\nresources → E005/E010/E013). Documentation Support is listed as required and the\ndocs-authoring epic exists. Both conditional branches cover their stated bounded outcomes\n(A and B for E002 and E006).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64845,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7235745e7d45a0a","agent_id":"ac2507bfc800dc5e2","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"6089416b-910e-421e-90f2-48913eae9c76","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:31:02.384Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
