{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d4ad0b9b126c17c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 14\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\t---\n9\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n10\t\n11\tStrategy triage: **not below threshold** (L effort, 4 affected code components, 5 involved teams,\n12\tmultiple architecturally distinct work streams) and **not docs-only** (three of four affected\n13\tcomponents require code changes). Full decomposition follows.\n14\t\n15\tStaff Engineer / SME Input section is empty (template placeholder only) — no overrides to log.\n16\t\n17\t## Component Name Mappings\n18\t\n19\tCanonical RHAI Jira components (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) assigned to epics:\n20\t\n21\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n22\t| --- | --- | --- |\n23\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | New component; no architecture-context file exists (not yet in platform) |\n24\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | New component; no architecture-context file exists |\n25\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Existing platform root operator (architecture context: rhods-operator.md) |\n26\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Existing console (architecture context: odh-dashboard.md) |\n27\t| Docs workstream | Documentation | |\n28\t| QE workstream | QE | |\n29\t| OTEL trace sink question | Model and Agent Observability | |\n30\t\n31\tNew-component detection: neither kagenti-operator nor kagenti-extensions has an architecture\n32\tcontext file, so both get the new-component onboarding treatment (Rule 20). However, the\n33\tstrategy's dependency table states the midstream forks already exist\n34\t(`opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` — status \"Exists\"; `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` is\n35\tnamed as the build source), so **no `repo-onboarding` epics are generated** — the onboarding\n36\tchain starts at license validation and Konflux onboarding. Fork readiness (including whether the\n37\tkagenti-extensions fork actually exists and is synced) is verified by the upstream validation\n38\tInvestigation (E001); if a fork is missing, repo-onboarding work is added as remediation.\n39\t\n40\t## Epic List\n41\t\n42\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n43\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n44\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality, CRD stability, and midstream fork readiness | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Resolve Keycloak runtime dependency and ClientRegistrationController TP configuration | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n47\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Decide TP dashboard integration depth (project tab vs standalone navigation) | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component removal | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Resolve OTEL trace sink requirement from parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | Konflux onboarding: kagenti-operator image (FIPS Go build, UBI9) | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | Konflux onboarding: AuthBridge proxy sidecar image (FIPS Go build, UBI9) | Implementation | Kagenti | P1 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | License validation for kagenti midstream repositories | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries for disconnected install | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P1 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E012 | Dashboard BFF plugin, feature flag, and agent list view | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n56\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | QE test plan and E2E validation for kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P0 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Installation, upgrade, and agent image contract documentation | Implementation | Docs | P0 |\n58\t\n59\tMain-plan epics: 14. Critical path length: 5\n60\t(E001 → E010 → E011 → E013 → E014).\n61\t\n62\t## Dependency DAG\n63\t\n64\t```mermaid\n65\tgraph TD\n66\t    E001 --> E010\n67\t    E003 --> E010\n68\t    E005 --> E010\n69\t    E010 --> E011\n70\t    E010 --> E012\n71\t    E004 --> E012\n72\t    E010 --> E013\n73\t    E011 --> E013\n74\t    E001 --> E014\n75\t    E003 --> E014\n76\t    E007 --> E014\n77\t    E008 --> E014\n78\t    E009 --> E014\n79\t    E010 --> E014\n80\t    E011 --> E014\n81\t    E012 --> E014\n82\t    E013 --> E014\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\tRoots (no dependencies): E001, E002, E003, E004, E005, E006, E007, E008, E009.\n86\t\n87\tBranch epics (not main-plan nodes, excluded from the diagram and critical path):\n88\t\n89\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E015` — AuthBridge envoy + lite variant Konflux components\n90\t  (gated by E002, outcome B: all three variants needed for TP).\n91\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E016` — OTEL trace sink integration for agent telemetry\n92\t  (gated by E006, outcome B: OTEL trace sink confirmed as a TP requirement).\n93\t\n94\t## DAG Justification\n95\t\n96\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n97\t| --- | --- | --- |\n98\t| E001 → E010 | Rule 3 | Upstream functional gaps or CRD instability change which controllers/manifests the component controller pins and deploys (rewrite gate) |\n99\t| E003 → E010 | Rule 3 | Whether ClientRegistrationController is enabled for TP (Keycloak dependency) changes the manifest overlays and deployed configuration |\n100\t| E005 → E010 | Rule 3 | Cross-namespace CRD/CR cleanup semantics change the garbage-collection logic the controller must implement |\n101\t| E010 → E011 | Rule 