{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b41749fe43befed4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E014\n3\ttitle: Installation, upgrade, and agent image contract documentation\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Documentation\n6\tteam: Docs\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: docs-authoring\n10\tdependencies:\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E007\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E008\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E009\n16\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n17\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E011\n18\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E012\n19\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E013\n20\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n21\tgate_failure_impact:\n22\t  action: add_remediation\n23\t  fallback_approach: If the Keycloak runtime-dependency resolution requires documenting\n24\t    an external prerequisite, additional prerequisite documentation content is added\n25\t    to this epic; the core installation and image-contract documentation is unchanged.\n26\tai_signals:\n27\t  change_specificity: 1\n28\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n29\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n30\t  existing_foundation: 1\n31\t  open_questions: -1\n32\t  external_dependency: 0\n33\t  human_process_gates: -1\n34\t  repo_access: 1\n35\t  architecture_claims: 0\n36\tinvestigation_signals: null\n37\tai_implementability: Medium\n38\tai_implementability_score: 2\n39\tjira_key: null\n40\tbranch: null\n41\t---\n42\t# Installation, upgrade, and agent image contract documentation\n43\t\n44\t## Description\n45\t\n46\tAuthor the customer-facing documentation for the Tech Preview kagenti-operator component:\n47\tinstallation and upgrade via the DataScienceCluster CR (opt-in enablement), the minimal image\n48\tcontract for creating a discoverable agent (endpoint format, health check, card structure), and\n49\tany external prerequisites (e.g., Keycloak, if the runtime-dependency decision requires it).\n50\t\n51\t## Description of upstream dependencies\n52\t\n53\tThis epic documents what was built, so it is blocked by all implementation work in the\n54\tstrategy (operator and AuthBridge builds, license clearance, the DSC component controller, CSV\n55\tpackaging, the dashboard agent views, and the QE validation) and by the upstream validation and\n56\tKeycloak dependency resolutions that determine its content.\n57\t\n58\t## Scope\n59\t\n60\t- Installation documentation: enabling kagenti-operator via the DSC (`managementState:\n61\t  Managed`), the Tech Preview opt-in default, and disablement with cleanup behavior.\n62\t- Minimal image contract documentation: the well-known capability-description endpoint format,\n63\t  health check, and card structure agents must expose to be discoverable.\n64\t- Upgrade documentation for the TP component (defaults to Removed, so existing clusters are\n65\t  unaffected).\n66\t- External prerequisite documentation as determined by the Keycloak runtime-dependency\n67\t  decision.\n68\t- Technically reviewed against the implemented behavior before publication.\n69\t\n70\t## Acceptance Criteria\n71\t\n72\t- Documentation covers the minimal image contract for creating a discoverable agent (endpoint\n73\t  format, health check, card structure), with the contract finalized against the validated\n74\t  operator behavior.\n75\t- Documentation covers DSC-based installation, opt-in enablement, upgrade, and disablement\n76\t  cleanup semantics.\n77\t- All documentation is technically reviewed against the implementation and passes the Red Hat\n78\t  docs content process.\n79\t- Keycloak (or any other confirmed external prerequisite) is documented if required.\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- Covers the strategy MUST acceptance criterion \"Documentation covers the minimal image\n84\t  contract for creating a discoverable agent (endpoint format, health check, card structure)\".\n85\t- Supports the P0 HLRs for DSC enablement and TP opt-in by documenting the enablement path.\n86\t"}]},"parent_t