{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-b75af42f-ead4-4948-9504-503409f4e852","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aeac05a7381440b8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b6wumj_a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017.md","content":"# ClusterServiceVersion entries for additional AuthBridge variants\n\n## Description\n\nConditional branch (outcome B of the AuthBridge variant-set investigation): if the TP variant\ndecision requires AuthBridge sidecar variants beyond the default `authbridge-proxy`\n(`authbridge-envoy` and/or `authbridge-lite`), add the corresponding SHA256-pinned\n`RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries to the rhods-operator ClusterServiceVersion so the additional\nsidecar images resolve for disconnected/air-gapped installation with image mirroring.\n\nThis is rhods-operator CSV packaging work owned by the Platform / ODH Operator team — the same\ncomponent/team boundary the main plan draws between Konflux onboarding (Kagenti-owned) and CSV\npackaging (Platform-owned). It extends the main-plan CSV packaging for the kagenti component:\nit adds entries to the ClusterServiceVersion that work produces. The image digests it pins are\nconfiguration references supplied at execution time by the Konflux builds of the additional\nvariants — availability is an acceptance criterion, not a scheduling dependency, so this work\nruns in parallel with the Konflux onboarding of those variants.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a SHA256-pinned `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entry to the ClusterServiceVersion for each additional\n  AuthBridge variant required by the TP decision (`authbridge-envoy`, `authbridge-lite`).\n- Validate the CSV renders correctly with the existing packaging tooling.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a disconnected RHOAI installation using image mirroring, when the kagenti component is\n  `Managed` and additional AuthBridge variants are required for TP, then each additional\n  variant image resolves from the mirrored registry via its `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entry, measured\n  by the variant images pulling from the mirror registry.\n- Pinned image digests for the additional variant images are available from their Konflux\n  builds at packaging time (configuration reference gate).\n- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- Extends the P1 HLR \"OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries for disconnected\n  installation\" to the additional AuthBridge variants required by the TP decision (the same\n  decision that extends the P1 AuthBridge Konflux HLR to the additional variants).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":59937,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b27480a9e843f94f","agent_id":"a919f34342319a63d","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"6d4413ef-e9bd-45da-a232-8800d984421d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:39:40.972Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
