012 | Dashboard BFF plugin, feature flag, and agent list view | Implementation | Dashboard | P1 |\n57\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E013 | QE test plan and E2E validation for kagenti component lifecycle | Implementation | QE | P0 |\n58\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E014 | Installation, upgrade, and agent image contract documentation | Implementation | Docs | P0 |\n59\t\n60\tMain-plan epics: 14. Critical path length: 5\n61\t(E001 → E010 → E011 → E013 → E014).\n62\t\n63\t## Dependency DAG\n64\t\n65\t```mermaid\n66\tgraph TD\n67\t    E001 --> E010\n68\t    E003 --> E010\n69\t    E005 --> E010\n70\t    E010 --> E011\n71\t    E010 --> E012\n72\t    E004 --> E012\n73\t    E010 --> E013\n74\t    E011 --> E013\n75\t    E001 --> E014\n76\t    E003 --> E014\n77\t    E007 --> E014\n78\t    E008 --> E014\n79\t    E009 --> E014\n80\t    E010 --> E014\n81\t    E011 --> E014\n82\t    E012 --> E014\n83\t    E013 --> E014\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\tRoots (no dependencies): E001, E002, E003, E004, E005, E006, E007, E008, E009.\n87\t\n88\tBranch epics (not main-plan nodes, excluded from the diagram and critical path):\n89\t\n90\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E015` — AuthBridge envoy + lite variant Konflux components\n91\t  (gated by E002, outcome B: all three variants needed for TP). Konflux onboarding only,\n92\t  Kagenti-owned; the CSV entries for the additional variants are NOT part of this epic.\n93\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017` — ClusterServiceVersion `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries for the\n94\t  additional AuthBridge variants (gated by E002, outcome B). Platform / ODH Operator-owned\n95\t  rhods-operator CSV packaging work, mirroring the main-plan E008/E011 boundary between\n96\t  Konflux onboarding (Kagenti) and CSV packaging (Platform).\n97\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E016` — OTEL trace sink wiring for agent telemetry (gated by E006,\n98\t  outcome B: OTEL trace sink confirmed as a TP requirement). Code implementation only.\n99\t- `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E018` — Trace sink configuration customer documentation (gated by\n100\t  E006, outcome B). Docs-authoring work separated from the wiring per the work-product\n101\t  boundary; the main-plan docs epic E014 does not cover this content (no dependency on E006).\n102\t\n103\tBranch epic relationships to main-plan work (documented here and in the epic bodies; branch\n104\tepics are plan documents excluded from the main-plan DAG, and their `dependencies` carry only\n105\tthe gating Investigation plus same-branch siblings):\n106\t\n107\t- BRANCH-B-E015's Konflux builds produce the image digests that BRANCH-B-E017 pins as CSV\n108\t  entries — a configuration-reference coupling enforced by BRANCH-B-E017's\n109\t  pinned-digest-availability AC, never a DAG edge (Rule 13/25; Rule 10 additionally forbids\n110\t  edges between konflux-onboarding and general implementation epics in either direction).\n111\t- BRANCH-B-E016 builds on the productized kagenti-operator component deployed by the\n112\t  component controller work (E010) and is validated against it.\n113\t- BRANCH-B-E017 extends the main-plan CSV packaging (E011): it adds entries to the\n114\t  ClusterServiceVersion that E011 produces.\n115\t- BRANCH-B-E018 is blocked by the trace sink wiring (BRANCH-B-E016), modeled as a same-branch\n116\t  dependency in its frontmatter `dependencies`.\n117\t\n118\t## DAG Justification\n119\t\n120\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n121\t| --- | --- | --- |\n122\t| E001 → E010 | Rule 3 | Upstream functional gaps or CRD instability change which controllers/manifests the component controller pins and deploys (rewrite gate) |\n123\t| E003 → E010 | Rule 3 | Whether ClientRegistrationController is enabled for TP (Keycloak dependency) changes the manifest overlays and deployed configuration |\n124\t| E005 → E010 | Rule 3 | Cross-namespace CRD/CR cleanup semantics change the garbage-collection logic the controller must implement |\n125\t| E010 → E011 | Rule 13 | The CSV declares the KagentiOperator component CRD and RBAC produced by the controller work — build-against artifact |\n126\t| E010 → E012 | Rule 13 | The dashboard feature flag is gated by the DSC kagenti component state — the dashboard builds against the component CR/schema created by the controller work |\n127\t| E004 → E012 | Rule 3 | Tab-in-project-view vs standalone navigation rewrites the dashboard BFF/UI scope (~1 vs ~2 sprints) |\n128\t| E010 → E013 | Rule 12 | Component-lifecycle E2E tests build against the controller's Managed/Removed behavior |\n129\t| E011 → E013 | Rule 12 | Disconnected-install validation exercises the CSV RELATED_IMAGE entries |\n130\t| E001 → E014 | Rule 3 / 11 | Docs must describe a validated image contract and stable CRD; docs are last |\n131\t| E003 → E014 | Rule 3 | Keycloak external-dependency documentation content depends on the resolution |\n132\t| E007 → E014 | Rule 11 | docs-authoring blocked by all Implementation epics |\n133\t| E008 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n134\t| E009 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n135\t| E010 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n136\t| E011 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n137\t| E012 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n138\t| E013 → E014 | Rule 11 | Same |\n139\t\n140\tDeliberate **non-edges** (Rule 10 / Rule 13 configuration-reference exception):\n141\t\n142\t- No edge from the Konflux onboarding epics (E007, E008, BRANCH-B-E015) to the component\n143\t  controller (E010), CSV packaging (E011), QE (E013), or the CSV branch epic\n144\t  (BRANCH-B-E017). The Konflux-built image digests are configuration\n145\t  references filled in at execution time; the coupling is enforced by acceptance criteria\n146\t  (\"Konflux-built image with SHA256-pinned digest available\") on the consuming epics, never by\n147\t  DAG dependencies. Wiring such edges would serialize work that must run in parallel.\n148\t- No edge between license validation (E009) and Konflux onboarding (E007/E008) — Rule 7/8:\n149\t  parallel start. Rule 9 (license → general implementation serial) has no target here: this\n150\t  strategy contains no general-purpose implementation epic built on the kagenti code (runtime\n151\t  features are out of scope, tracked in RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589). A license failure would\n152\t  remediate dependency sets inside the Konflux/Dockerfile work, not change epic structure.\n153\t- No repo-onboarding epic: midstream forks already exist per the strategy dependency table.\n154\t\n155\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n156\t\n157\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n158\t| --- | --- | --- |\n159\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E007 |\n160\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern | P0 | E010 |\n161\t| `managementState: Removed` cleans up all operator-managed resources | P0 | E010 (semantics informed by E005) |\n162\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E007, E008, E009 (process constraint on all Kagenti midstream work) |\n163\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E010 |\n164\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin + feature flag | P1 | E012 |\n165\t| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected install | P1 | E011 (+ BRANCH-B-E017 if additional AuthBridge variants are required for TP) |\n166\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E008 (+ BRANCH-B-E015 for additional variants) |\n167\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if free) | P2 | E007, E008 (build-configuration acceptance criteria, not separate epics — incidental to the same build work) |\n168\t\n169\tAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements; no epic without HLR (or strategy-AC) trace.\n170\t\n171\tStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage notes:\n172\t\n173\t- DSC enablement, Removed cleanup, documentation MUSTs → E010, E005, E014.\n174\t- Console/API discovery of agents → E012 (TP read-only agent list).\n175\t- AgentRuntime CR selection/discovery, metadata sync on rollouts, degraded condition (SHOULD),\n176\t  Deployment-deletion garbage collection → upstream operator runtime behavior, explicitly out of\n177\t  scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588). Not covered by design.\n178\t- Sandbox auto-registration (COULD) → out of scope; see Health Warnings.\n179\t- OTEL trace sink (open MUST from parent RFE) → E006 + BRANCH-B-E016 (wiring) +\n180\t  BRANCH-B-E018 (customer documentation).\n181\t\n182\t## Health Warnings\n183\t\n184\t1. **Open parent-RFE MUST (OTEL trace sink)** — the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries an OTEL\n185\t   trace sink MUST not reflected in this strategy's HLRs; under team discussion. Modeled as\n186\t   Investigation E006 with conditional branch epics BRANCH-B-E016 (wiring) and BRANCH-B-E018\n187\t   (customer documentation). If the discussion lands late, TP docs and QE scope shift.\n188\t2. **Dashboard architecture-context discrepancy** — architecture context (odh-dashboard.md,\n189\t   RHOAI 3.6-ea.1) shows an existing `agent-ops` federated BFF module with per-agent RBAC that\n190\t   the strategy does not mention (it cites only 7 plugins / ports 8043-8643). The dashboard epic\n191\t   must reconcile reuse/extension of the existing agent-ops module against building a new kagenti\n192\t   plugin before committing to a new BFF container and port.\n193\t3. **COULD acceptance criterion (sandbox auto-registration) uncovered** — runtime behavior out of\n194\t   scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7589), and the OpenShell Sandbox CR interplay open question remains with\n195\t   the Kagenti team. Intentional gap; flagged so review does not treat it as an omission.\n196\t4. **Minimal image contract undecided (A2A vs simpler format)** — owned by RHAIRFE-7588; the\n197\t   documentation epic carries it as an acceptance criterion (contract finalized and documented),\n198\t   not an Investigation here, because no epic in this strategy changes existence/approach based\n199\t   on the answer.\n200\t5. **kagenti-extensions midstream fork existence assumed** — the strategy references\n201\t   `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` as the build source but only lists the operator fork as\n202\t   confirmed. Verified by E001; if missing, repo-onboarding is added (add_remediation).\n203\t6. **Konflux pipeline capacity (\"Needs submission\")** — lead-time risk on the critical path to\n204\t   the 3.5 release. The Konflux epics are DAG roots precisely so onboarding submission starts\n205\t   immediately, per the strategy's own risk mitigation.\n206\t7. **Docs epic (P0 via strategy priority Critical) is blocked by P1 dashboard and CSV epics** —\n207\t   intentional consequence of the docs-last rule (docs describe what was built); not a priority\n208\t   inversion to fix.\n209\t8. **Strategy data-quality note** — a proposed AC references CRD\n210\t   `agentrimes.agent.kagenti.dev` (apparent typo for `agentruntimes.agent.kagenti.dev`); worth\n211\t   correcting during PM/Engineering validation of the proposed ACs.\n212\t9. **No scope traps detected** — NFRs (FIPS, container security, disconnected install) map to\n213\t   acceptance criteria on the Konflux/packaging epics and do not imply nonexistent\n214\t   infrastructure; out-of-scope items are consistent with the NFRs.\n215\t\n216\t## Tiered Delivery\n217\t\n218\tNot applicable. The external dependencies (upstream kagenti-operator and kagenti-extensions)\n219\talready exist and are functional per the dependency table; no dependency with uncertain timing\n220\tgates a user-facing deliverable. The only timing risk (Konflux capacity) is an internal lead-time\n221\titem mitigated by starting the onboarding epics as DAG roots.\n222\t\n223\t## Conditional Decomposition Branches\n224\t\n225\t**E002 — AuthBridge variant set for TP** (bounded, 2 outcomes):\n226\t\n227\t- Outcome A (proxy only for TP): main plan stands as-is; the AuthBridge proxy Konflux epic\n228\t  (E008) is the complete variant scope. No branch epic.\n229\t- Outcome B (envoy and/or lite also needed for 3.5): `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E015` adds the\n230\t  additional Konflux components (Kagenti-owned), and `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E017` adds the\n231\t  corresponding CSV `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries (Platform / ODH Operator-owned) — mirroring the\n232\t  main-plan E008/E011 boundary between Konflux onboarding and CSV packaging.\n233\t\n234\t**E006 — OTEL trace sink requirement** (bounded, 2 outcomes):\n235\t\n236\t- Outcome A (not required for TP / deferred): no additional work; main plan stands.\n237\t- Outcome B (confirmed TP requirement per parent RFE MUST):\n238\t  `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E016` adds the OTEL trace sink / telemetry auto-configuration\n239\t  wiring (code implementation), and `RHAISTRAT-8006-BRANCH-B-E018` covers its customer\n240\t  documentation as a separate docs-authoring work item (the main-plan docs epic E014 has no\n241\t  dependency on this requirement and does not cover the content).\n242\t\n243\tBranch epics are attached to their gating Investigations as plan documents; they are excluded\n244\tfrom the main-plan critical path.\n245\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b09d530114d28c8","agent_id":"a8a4c6b9da1a738b7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"cab43e3b-42ef-4337-8524-f758325d46d9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:42:52.598Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a51a2267c6b302e4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
