{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a003f22a3a645ed5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E005\n3\ttitle: Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component removal\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 1\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -1\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Medium\n19\tai_implementability_score: 0\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component removal\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThis investigation resolves what happens to user-created AgentRuntime CRs when the kagenti\n30\tcomponent is disabled via the DataScienceCluster. The component controller cleans up\n31\toperator-managed resources in `redhat-ods-applications`, but user-created AgentRuntime CRs in\n32\tother namespaces may become orphaned. The Platform / ODH Operator team must decide whether\n33\tcomponent removal includes cross-namespace CRD deletion (which destroys user-created CRs) or\n34\tleaves them orphaned, and document the chosen semantics so the controller's garbage-collection\n35\tlogic implements a defined behavior.\n36\t\n37\t## Scope\n38\t\n39\t- Decide the removal semantics: delete the AgentRuntime CRD cluster-wide (removing user CRs in\n40\t  all namespaces) versus leaving user-created CRs in place on component removal.\n41\t- Evaluate how existing platform component controllers handle analogous cases and whether a\n42\t  finalizer-based enumeration of owned resources is needed.\n43\t- Record the decision and the concrete cleanup contract (resource list, namespace scope,\n44\t  ordering) the component controller must implement.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Decision recorded with rationale, covering: controller Deployment, RBAC (ClusterRoles,\n49\t  ClusterRoleBindings, Roles, RoleBindings), the AgentRuntime CRD, the mutating webhook\n50\t  configuration, namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications`, and user-created\n51\t  AgentRuntime CRs in other namespaces.\n52\t- The cleanup contract is specified precisely enough to implement and to test in E2E (resources\n53\t  in multiple namespaces).\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- Qualifies the P0 HLR \"When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed\n58\t  resources are cleaned up\": the answer defines what \"all\" means for cross-namespace user\n59\t  resources and changes the controller's garbage-collection scope.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b09d530114d28c8","agent_id":"a8a4c6b9da1a738b7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"28414ec9-eedd-491f-a87b-d82fccd119b9","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:43:06.428Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a003f22a3a645ed5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
