{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-88724a9efc2d0ab4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E007\n3\ttitle: 'Konflux onboarding: kagenti-operator image (FIPS Go build, UBI9)'\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Agentic\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\timplementation_type: konflux-onboarding\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: -1\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Konflux onboarding: kagenti-operator image (FIPS Go build, UBI9)\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tOnboard the kagenti-operator container image to the Konflux build pipeline from the\n34\t`opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` midstream fork, with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on a UBI9\n35\tbase. This is the critical-path build-pipeline item for the 3.5 release and should be submitted\n36\timmediately (the Konflux onboarding request has lead time).\n37\t\n38\t## Scope\n39\t\n40\t- Convert the kagenti-operator Dockerfile to the multi-stage pattern used by other RHOAI Go\n41\t  operators (builder stage compiles with `CGO_ENABLED=1` and\n42\t  `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`; production stage copies the binary onto\n43\t  `ubi9/ubi-minimal`), consistent with rhods-operator and model-registry-operator.\n44\t- Add `rpms.lock.yaml` for RPM lockfile pinning and `go.sum` for Go dependency locking.\n45\t- Create and submit the Konflux component for the kagenti-operator image; track submission\n46\t  status weekly against the code-complete deadline and escalate per the strategy's risk\n47\t  mitigation if submission is delayed.\n48\t- Ensure AMD64 architecture builds (arm64 only if the pipeline supports it without additional\n49\t  effort).\n50\t- Apply container security conventions: non-root execution (USER 65532:65532), capability\n51\t  dropping, `seccompProfile.type: RuntimeDefault`.\n52\t- Follow the upstream-first policy: significant changes (e.g., Dockerfile restructuring) go to\n53\t  the `kagenti/*` upstream repos before being pulled into the `opendatahub-io/*` midstream fork.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The kagenti-operator container image passes the Konflux build pipeline `check-payload`\n58\t  validation for FIPS compliance (binary linked against OpenSSL, no statically-linked Go\n59\t  crypto).\n60\t- The Konflux build is green and produces a SHA256-pinned image digest consumable by the DSC\n61\t  component deployment and CSV packaging (configuration reference — no DAG dependency).\n62\t- Build supports AMD64; arm64 included only if achievable without additional effort.\n63\t\n64\t## HLR Traceability\n65\t\n66\t- P0: Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation\n67\t  (`GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`, `CGO_ENABLED=1`) on UBI9 base.\n68\t- P0: Upstream-first policy (changes to `kagenti/*` before `opendatahub-io/*` midstream forks).\n69\t- P2: Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required for TP; arm64 if pipeline supports it without\n70\t  additional effort).\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b09d530114d28c8","agent_id":"a8a4c6b9da1a738b7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"017b499e-7492-478a-9243-b0b1d5e7e081","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:43:08.578Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-88724a9efc2d0ab4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
