{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b158f25fb5cadbaa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E012\n3\ttitle: Dashboard BFF plugin, feature flag, and agent list view\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E004\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the integration-depth decision lands on the other option (project\n16\t    tab vs standalone navigation), the dashboard BFF and UI scope must be rewritten\n17\t    to match the chosen surface before implementation.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 4\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Dashboard BFF plugin, feature flag, and agent list view\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tRegister a kagenti dashboard plugin in the odh-dashboard Module Federation architecture and\n40\tprovide Tech Preview agent visibility: a read-only list of AgentRuntime CRs with status and a\n41\tlink to workload details. A Go BFF sidecar proxies Kubernetes API requests for AgentRuntime CR\n42\tmanagement, and a feature flag hides all agent-related UI when the kagenti component is Removed\n43\tin the DSC.\n44\t\n45\t## Description of upstream dependencies\n46\t\n47\tThis epic is gated on the UX/PM decision on TP integration depth (project tab vs standalone\n48\tnavigation), which rewrites its scope. It also builds on the DSC kagenti component state\n49\tsurface created by the rhods-operator component controller work, which the feature flag reads.\n50\t\n51\t## Scope\n52\t\n53\t- Add a `disableKagenti` feature flag (or equivalent) to the `OdhDashboardConfig` CR, gated by\n54\t  the DSC kagenti component state: when the component is `Removed`, all agent-related UI\n55\t  elements are hidden.\n56\t- Implement the kagenti BFF as a Go sidecar container in the dashboard pod following the\n57\t  established federated-module pattern (dedicated TLS port with Bearer token authentication),\n58\t  allocating the next available port in the 8043-8743 range and verifying against current\n59\t  assignments.\n60\t- Implement the TP agent list view (list AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible\n61\t  namespaces, show status, link to workload details) per the decided integration depth.\n62\t- Before building a new BFF container, reconcile against the existing agent-ops federated\n63\t  module already present in the odh-dashboard architecture (architecture context,\n64\t  odh-dashboard.md): extend it if it covers the needed surface, otherwise build the new plugin\n65\t  and document why.\n66\t- Full agent management UI is out of scope (read-only visibility only).\n67\t\n68\t## Acceptance Criteria\n69\t\n70\t- Given the dashboard deployed with the feature flag active, when a user navigates to the agent\n71\t  views, the dashboard displays AgentRuntime CRs from the user's accessible namespaces,\n72\t  measured by the view rendering data retrieved via the BFF API proxy.\n73\t- When the kagenti component is `Removed` in the DSC, all agent-related UI elements are hidden.\n74\t- The chosen port does not collide with existing BFF sidecar assignments.\n75\t- UX design for the chosen integration depth (tab vs standalone section) is finalized and\n76\t  implemented.\n77\t\n78\t## HLR Traceability\n79\t\n80\t- P1: Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin registration and feature flag for agent\n81\t  views.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b09d53