ned\ncomponents are canonical (Agentic, AI Core Platform, AI Core Dashboard, Documentation, QE,\nModel and Agent Observability). The Konflux-onboarding vs CSV-packaging split across the\nKagenti/Platform boundary is applied consistently in both the main plan (E008/E011) and the\nbranch (E015/E017). No scope duplication between siblings (E007/E008 are distinct images;\nE011/E017 add disjoint CSV entries; E014/E018 cover disjoint doc content). No work-product\nmixing: docs-authoring work is separated from code (E014, E018) and the branch separates\nwiring (E016) from its documentation (E018).\n\nHowever, E010 is clearly oversized. The strategy's own effort estimate prices the\nrhods-operator component-controller workstream at 2-3 sprints (component CRD definition, DSC\nschema extension, controller action pipeline, registry registration, kustomize manifest\nintegration, full Managed/Removed lifecycle, manifest overlays) — and even with testing moved\nto E013 and CSV packaging moved to E011, E010 still carries multiple sprints of work in a\nsingle epic, well beyond the ~2-week epic guideline. A split is feasible along the\ndeploy-vs-Removed-cleanup axis: the strategy itself treats cleanup semantics as a separable\nconcern with its own Investigation (E005), its own risk row, and its own NFR. Major issue —\nscore 0.\n\n### 4. Type Correctness (1/2)\n\nAll six Investigations genuinely change downstream structure (manifest baseline rewrite,\nvariant-set branch, Keycloak configuration, dashboard scope rewrite, cleanup semantics, OTEL\nrequirement branch) and each has downstream dependents; all Implementations produce concrete\nartifacts. Every `gated_by` target appears in the epic's direct `dependencies`, and every\npopulated `gate_failure_impact` has both `action` and `fallback_approach` describing a real\nchange on gate failure.\n\nGating-metadata gap (two instances of the same finding): `gated_by` is under-populated\nrelative to the Investigation dependencies.\n\n- E010 d