sible; the rationale is misattributed/thin — score 1.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (0/2)\n\nACs are otherwise specific and testable: Given/When/Then with kubectl-measurable outcomes on\nE010; decision gates expressed as ACs; digest-availability configuration-reference gates per\nRule 13; no epic body references sibling epics by draft ID. Docs epics carry the Rule 24\ntechnical-review AC (E014, E018). Konflux epics carry green-build ACs (E007, E008,\nBRANCH-B-E015), and E010 carries \"Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux)\".\n\nBut two epics that change Konflux-built repositories are missing the Rule 25 \"build pipeline\ngreen\" AC:\n\n- E011 adds `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries plus the KagentiOperator CRD/RBAC declarations to the\n  rhods-operator ClusterServiceVersion — the same repository as E010 and the same work class\n  as branch twin BRANCH-B-E017, both of which carry \"Build pipeline green for rhods-operator\n  changes (Konflux)\". E011 has three ACs, none about the build pipeline.\n- E012 implements a new Go BFF container and feature flag in odh-dashboard — a Konflux-built\n  repository per architecture context (Dockerfile.konflux, per-BFF Dockerfile.konflux.*\n  files) — and has no build-pipeline AC at all.\n\nMultiple missing rule-mandated ACs — major, score 0. The rule applies to every epic that\nmeets its criteria, not just the most obvious one.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n\nFull scope coverage: every strategy workstream maps to epics (Konflux onboarding E007/E008\nplus BRANCH-B-E015, component controller E010, CSV packaging E011 plus BRANCH-B-E017,\ndashboard E012, QE E013, docs E014 plus BRANCH-B-E018); all six strategy open questions have\ncorresponding Investigations; the open parent-RFE OTEL MUST is modeled as Investigation E006\nwith conditional wiring (BRANCH-B-E016) and documentation (BRANCH-B-E018) branches covering\nboth bounded outcomes. Risks are carried into epic scope/ACs (Konflux lead time on E007,\nwebhook ordering on E013, port collision on E012, orphaned resources on E005/E010/E013).\nDocumentation Support: Yes is honored with docs-authoring epic E014 (Rule 11). Out-of-scope\nitems are consistently fenced to RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589/7408, with intentional gaps flagged in\nhealth warnings rather than silently dropped. Skipping repo-onboarding for the new components\nis justified by the strategy's dependency table (midstream fork status \"Exists\") and backstopped\nby E001's fork-readiness verification with a documented remediation path.\n\nMinor: E008's scope omits the container-security NFR conventions (non-root USER 65532,\ncapability dropping, seccompProfile.type: RuntimeDefault) that E007 explicitly carries,\nalthough the NFR applies to all Go operator/sidecar images; E012's new BFF image build wiring\n(Dockerfile.konflux pattern) is implicit in \"following the established federated-module\npattern\" rather than explicit scope.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":80156,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b09d530114d28c8","agent_id":"a8a4c6b9da1a738b7","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"cf10b111-f3d6-433a-9ea3-7b827d84c78d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:59:28.455Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8006 decomposition"}
