omposition is otherwise strong: the DAG is\n70\tfully consistent, konflux/general parallelism is handled correctly everywhere, HLR coverage is\n71\tcomplete, and conditional branches are well formed. The failures are a clearly oversized epic\n72\tand missing rule-mandated acceptance criteria, both fixable without restructuring the plan.\n73\t\n74\t## Criterion Details\n75\t\n76\t### 1. HLR Coverage (2/2)\n77\t\n78\tAll 9 HLRs map to epics and the traceability matrix is present and consistent with each epic's\n79\tHLR Traceability section: P0s to E007/E009/E010, P1s to E008/E011/E012, and the P2 multi-arch\n80\tHLR is covered as build-configuration acceptance criteria on E007/E008 — incidental to the same\n81\tbuild work, correctly not split into separate epics. Priority inheritance is sound: the P0\n82\tInvestigations (E001, E003, E005) gate the P0 controller epic (E010); E010 (P0) enabling P1\n83\tepics (E011, E012) is not an inversion. Docs epics E014/E018 are P0 per the docs-authoring\n84\texemption (strategy priority Critical → P0) and are not flagged for depending on P1\n85\timplementations.\n86\t\n87\tStrategy acceptance criteria are correctly parceled: runtime-behavior MUSTs (AgentRuntime\n88\tselection, metadata sync, degraded condition, Deployment-deletion GC) are explicitly out of\n89\tscope per RHAIRFE-7587/7588 and flagged in health warnings rather than silently dropped; the\n90\tCOULD sandbox criterion is flagged as an intentional gap.\n91\t\n92\tMinor: BRANCH-B-E016 is P0 while its gating Investigation E006 is P1. If the parent RFE's OTEL\n93\ttrace sink MUST is confirmed for TP, P0 wiring sits behind a P1 investigation. E006 does not\n94\tblock main-plan P0 work, so this is not a blocking inversion, but E006 should be raised to P0\n95\tor carry an explicit escalation note.\n96\t\n97\t### 2. DAG Coherence (2/2)\n98\t\n99\tThe `graph TD` diagram (dependency → dependent) matches every epic's frontmatter\n100\t`dependencies` exactly in both directions; no