pic built on the kagenti code (runtime\n150\t  features are out of scope, tracked in RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589). A license failure would\n151\t  remediate dependency sets inside the Konflux/Dockerfile work, not change epic structure.\n152\t- No repo-onboarding epic: midstream forks already exist per the strategy dependency table.\n153\t\n154\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n155\t\n156\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n157\t| --- | --- | --- |\n158\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E007 |\n159\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern | P0 | E010 |\n160\t| `managementState: Removed` cleans up all operator-managed resources | P0 | E010 (semantics informed by E005) |\n161\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E007, E008, E009 (process constraint on all Kagenti midstream work) |\n162\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E010 |\n163\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin + feature flag | P1 | E012 |\n164\t| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected install | P1 | E011 (+ BRANCH-B-E017 if additional AuthBridge variants are required for TP) |\n165\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E008 (+ BRANCH-B-E015 for additional variants) |\n166\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if free) | P2 | E007, E008 (build-configuration acceptance criteria, not separate epics — incidental to the same build work) |\n167\t\n168\tAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements; no epic without HLR (or strategy-AC) trace.\n169\t\n170\tStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage notes:\n171\t\n172\t- DSC enablement, Removed cleanup, documentation MUSTs → E010, E005, E014.\n173\t- Console/API discovery of agents → E012 (TP read-only agent list).\n174\t- AgentRuntime CR selection/discovery, metadata sync on rollouts, degraded condition (SHOULD),\n175\t  D