{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a26ee10ee02d8e2c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E005\n13\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n14\tgate_failure_impact:\n15\t  action: rewrite\n16\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream validation finds functional gaps or an unstable\n17\t    AgentRuntime CRD, the manifest baseline and possibly the controller scope (e.g.,\n18\t    deferred MLflowReconciler / ClientRegistrationController per negotiated TP scope\n19\t    reduction) must be rewritten before the component controller work can proceed.\n20\tai_signals:\n21\t  change_specificity: 1\n22\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n23\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n24\t  existing_foundation: 1\n25\t  open_questions: -1\n26\t  external_dependency: 0\n27\t  human_process_gates: -1\n28\t  repo_access: 1\n29\t  architecture_claims: 1\n30\timplementation_type: null\n31\tinvestigation_signals: null\n32\tai_implementability: High\n33\tai_implementability_score: 4\n34\tjira_key: null\n35\tbranch: null\n36\t---\n37\t# KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tRegister kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator component\n42\tregistry, following the established 16-component pattern. This delivers the DataScienceCluster\n43\t(CSC/DSC) enablement path: a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD, a component controller\n44\timplementing the standard action pipeline, kustomize manifest integration from the midstream\n45\tfork, and the full `managementState: Managed/Removed` lifecycle with Tech Preview opt-in\n46\t(defaults to Removed).\n47\t\n48\t## Description of upstream dependencies\n49\t\n50\tThis epic is gated on three resolved unknowns: the upstream validation of the kagenti-operator\n51\t(controllers present, CRD stable, baseline manifest commit pinned), the Keycloak /\n52\tClientRegistrationController TP configuration decision, and the AgentRuntime CR cleanup\n53\tsemantics decision. Each changes what the manifests and controller must do, so the epic starts\n54\tonce they are resolved.\n55\t\n56\t## Scope\n57\t\n58\t- Define the `KagentiOperator` kind in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`\n59\t  group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, and other component CRDs, and\n60\t  extend the DSC CR schema accordingly.\n61\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases,\n62\t  kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect) and register it in the\n63\t  component registry.\n64\t- Integrate kustomize manifests from the midstream fork at pinned commits (via the standard\n65\t  manifest-fetch script) into the prefetched-manifests layout, with RHOAI-specific overlays for\n66\t  namespace (`redhat-ods-applications`), image references, and RBAC adjustments.\n67\t- Implement `managementState` lifecycle: `Managed` deploys the operator (Deployment, CRDs,\n68\t  RBAC, mutating webhook); `Removed` deletes all operator-managed resources — controller\n69\t  Deployment, ClusterRoles/ClusterRoleBindings/Roles/RoleBindings, the AgentRuntime CRD, the\n70\t  mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources in `redhat-ods-applications` —\n71\t  per the decided cleanup semantics (including the cross-namespace CR handling decision).\n72\t- Default the component to `Removed` (explicit opt-in) for Tech Preview.\n73\t- Apply the decided TP configuration for the ClientRegistrationController / Keycloak dependency\n74\t  in the manifest overlays.\n75\t\n76\t## Acceptance Criteria\n77\t\n78\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti component `managementState: Managed`, when\n79\t  the DSC controller reconciles, the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in\n80\t  `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image (SHA256-pinned digest available as a\n81\t  configuration reference), measured by a Ready deployment with `app=kagenti-operator`.\n82\t- Given the component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the controller reconciles, all\n83\t  operator-managed resources are deleted per the decided cleanup contract (verified for\n84\t  resources in multiple namespaces), measured by no remaining Deployment and the AgentRuntime\n85\t  CRD returning not found.\n86\t- Component defaults to `Removed` (opt-in); existing clusters are unaffected by upgrade.\n87\t- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n88\t- Manifests are pinned to the validated upstream/midstream baseline commit.\n89\t- The Keycloak / ClientRegistrationController TP configuration decision is resolved and its\n90\t  outcome applied in the manifest overlays before this epic completes (decision gate on the\n91\t  Keycloak runtime-dependency investigation — this epic is blocked on that outcome).\n92\t- The AgentRuntime CR cleanup-semantics decision is resolved and the garbage-collection logic\n93\t  implements the decided cleanup contract before this epic completes (decision gate on the\n94\t  cleanup-semantics investigation — this epic is blocked on that outcome).\n95\t\n96\t## HLR Traceability\n97\t\n98\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component\n99\t  controller pattern with `managementState: Managed/Removed`.\n100\t- P0: When disabled, all operator-managed resources are cleaned up (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs,\n101\t  namespace-scoped resources).\n102\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC).\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be364346b92c0a7e","agent_id":"a96bcd1a69cb8e30f","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed