{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fdf71ca2edcc80f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E006\n3\ttitle: Resolve OTEL trace sink requirement from parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451)\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: Model and Agent Observability\n6\tteam: Kagenti\n7\ttype: Investigation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tinvestigation_signals:\n10\t  question_specificity: 1\n11\t  source_accessibility: 0\n12\t  local_runnability: 0\n13\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n14\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n15\timplementation_type: null\n16\tdependencies: []\n17\tai_signals: null\n18\tai_implementability: Low\n19\tai_implementability_score: -1\n20\tjira_key: null\n21\tbranch: null\n22\tgated_by: null\n23\tgate_failure_impact: null\n24\t---\n25\t# Resolve OTEL trace sink requirement from parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451)\n26\t\n27\t## Description\n28\t\n29\tThe parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries a MUST for OTEL trace sink integration that is not yet\n30\treflected in this strategy's requirements and is under team discussion. This investigation\n31\tresolves whether OTEL trace sink integration is a Tech Preview requirement for the productized\n32\tkagenti-operator or is deferred. If it is confirmed as a TP requirement, a conditional branch\n33\tepic (telemetry auto-configuration / trace sink wiring) becomes active; if deferred, the main\n34\tplan is complete as decomposed.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- Conclude the team discussion on the parent RFE's OTEL trace sink MUST: in scope for TP, or\n39\t  deferred (and to which release/tracking ticket).\n40\t- If in scope, identify what the operator must auto-configure (trace sink endpoint wiring for\n41\t  agent workloads) and any dependency on the Agent Runtime Contract work tracked in RHAIRFE-7589.\n42\t- Record the decision with product-owner sign-off.\n43\t\n44\t## Acceptance Criteria\n45\t\n46\t- Decision recorded: OTEL trace sink integration required for TP (branch epic activated) or\n47\t  deferred (with tracking location for the deferred work).\n48\t- If required, the minimal TP scope of the trace sink integration is enumerated so the branch\n49\t  epic can be scheduled.\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- No current HLR maps to this question (that is the point: the parent RFE MUST is not yet\n54\t  reflected). The answer determines whether an additional requirement/epic enters this\n55\t  strategy's scope.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be364346b92c0a7e","agent_id":"a96bcd1a69cb8e30f","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"d6e8260a-0372-4982-87fd-fbc6e8dbbfdc","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:01:35.852Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fdf71ca2edcc80f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-8006"}
