Platform-owned). It extends the main-plan CSV packaging for the kagenti component:\n47\tit adds entries to the ClusterServiceVersion that work produces. The image digests it pins are\n48\tconfiguration references supplied at execution time by the Konflux builds of the additional\n49\tvariants — availability is an acceptance criterion, not a scheduling dependency, so this work\n50\truns in parallel with the Konflux onboarding of those variants.\n51\t\n52\t## Scope\n53\t\n54\t- Add a SHA256-pinned `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entry to the ClusterServiceVersion for each additional\n55\t  AuthBridge variant required by the TP decision (`authbridge-envoy`, `authbridge-lite`).\n56\t- Validate the CSV renders correctly with the existing packaging tooling.\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a disconnected RHOAI installation using image mirroring, when the kagenti component is\n61\t  `Managed` and additional AuthBridge variants are required for TP, then each additional\n62\t  variant image resolves from the mirrored registry via its `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entry, measured\n63\t  by the variant images pulling from the mirror registry.\n64\t- Pinned image digests for the additional variant images are available from their Konflux\n65\t  builds at packaging time (configuration reference gate).\n66\t- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n67\t\n68\t## HLR Traceability\n69\t\n70\t- Extends the P1 HLR \"OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` entries for disconnected\n71\t  installation\" to the additional AuthBridge variants required by the TP decision (the same\n72\t  decision that extends the P1 AuthBridge Konflux HLR to the additional variants).\n73\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be364346b92c0a7e","agent_id":"a96bcd1a69cb8e30f","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"aa91b3cd-75bb-4986-a2f7-c2e7ef286b5d","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:01:44.285Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8caa8ae2f9295842","permission_decision":{