{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-4199c381-89e8-4ef2-b23b-38aab15e1781","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-af15e5c1279273db","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8006-b6wumj_a/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8006-E019.md","content":"# KagentiOperator Removed-state cleanup and garbage collection in rhods-operator\n\n## Description\n\nImplement the `managementState: Removed` side of the KagentiOperator component lifecycle in\nrhods-operator: when the kagenti component is disabled in the DataScienceCluster, the component\ncontroller deletes all operator-managed resources per the decided cleanup contract. This is\nsplit out of the component-controller deploy workstream because the strategy prices the combined\ncontroller work at 2-3 sprints and cleanup semantics are a separable concern with their own\ninvestigation (the cleanup-semantics decision), their own risk row (orphaned resources on\ncomponent disable), and their own NFR (resource cleanup on disable).\n\n## Description of upstream dependencies\n\nThis epic is gated on the cleanup-semantics decision: whether component removal includes\ncross-namespace AgentRuntime CRD deletion (destroying user-created CRs) or leaves them in place\ndefines the garbage-collection contract this epic implements. It also builds on the component\ncontroller, `KagentiOperator` CRD, and registry registration delivered by the deploy-side\ncontroller work — the Removed transition is implemented in that controller.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement the `Managed` → `Removed` transition in the component controller: delete the\n  controller Deployment, ClusterRoles/ClusterRoleBindings/Roles/RoleBindings, the AgentRuntime\n  CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources (ConfigMaps, Secrets)\n  in `redhat-ods-applications`, per the decided cleanup contract.\n- Implement the decided cross-namespace AgentRuntime CR handling (cluster-wide CRD deletion\n  versus leaving user-created CRs in place), including a finalizer-based enumeration of owned\n  resources where the decided contract requires it (strategy risk: DSC component cleanup leaves\n  orphaned resources).\n- Apply the decided cleanup contract's resource list, namespace scope, and ordering exactly, so\n  the QE lifecycle validation can test it with resources in multiple namespaces.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the kagenti component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the component controller\n  reconciles the state change, all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook\n  configuration) are deleted per the decided cleanup contract, verified for resources in multiple\n  namespaces, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator`\n  returning no results and the AgentRuntime CRD returning not found.\n- The AgentRuntime CR cleanup-semantics decision is resolved and the garbage-collection logic\n  implements the decided cleanup contract before this epic completes (decision gate on the\n  cleanup-semantics investigation — this epic is blocked on that outcome).\n- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- P0: When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up:\n  controller Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":56647,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be364346b92c0a7e","agent_id":"a96bcd1a69cb8e30f","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"ae2a406f-bea4-4e04-b26e-ac97f3465737","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:06:00.088Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-8006"}
