{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fb65f559abb1a86","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n3\tepic_count: 15\n4\tcritical_path_length: 5\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-8006 ([TP] Productize & Downstream the Agent Operator)\n11\t\n12\tStrategy triage: **not below threshold** (L effort, 4 affected code components, 5 involved teams,\n13\tmultiple architecturally distinct work streams) and **not docs-only** (three of four affected\n14\tcomponents require code changes). Full decomposition follows.\n15\t\n16\tStaff Engineer / SME Input section is empty (template placeholder only) — no overrides to log.\n17\t\n18\t## Component Name Mappings\n19\t\n20\tCanonical RHAI Jira components (from `.context/rhai-components.txt`) assigned to epics:\n21\t\n22\t| Strategy component | Canonical component | Note |\n23\t| --- | --- | --- |\n24\t| kagenti-operator | Agentic | New component; no architecture-context file exists (not yet in platform) |\n25\t| kagenti-extensions (AuthBridge) | Agentic | New component; no architecture-context file exists |\n26\t| rhods-operator | AI Core Platform | Existing platform root operator (architecture context: rhods-operator.md) |\n27\t| odh-dashboard | AI Core Dashboard | Existing console (architecture context: odh-dashboard.md) |\n28\t| Docs workstream | Documentation | |\n29\t| QE workstream | QE | |\n30\t| OTEL trace sink question | Model and Agent Observability | |\n31\t\n32\tNew-component detection: neither kagenti-operator nor kagenti-extensions has an architecture\n33\tcontext file, so both get the new-component onboarding treatment (Rule 20). However, the\n34\tstrategy's dependency table states the midstream forks already exist\n35\t(`opendatahub-io/kagenti-operator` — status \"Exists\"; `opendatahub-io/kagenti-extensions` is\n36\tnamed as the build source), so **no `repo-onboarding` epics are generated** — the onboarding\n37\tchain starts at license validation and Konflux onboarding. Fork readiness (including whether the\n38\tkagenti-extensions fork actually exists and is synced) is verified by the upstream validation\n39\tInvestigation (E001); if a fork is missing, repo-onboarding work is added as remediation.\n40\t\n41\t## Epic List\n42\t\n43\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n44\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n45\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E001 | Validate upstream kagenti-operator functionality, CRD stability, and midstream fork readiness | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n46\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E002 | Determine AuthBridge sidecar variant set for Tech Preview | Investigation | Kagenti | P1 |\n47\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E003 | Resolve Keycloak runtime dependency and ClientRegistrationController TP configuration | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n48\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E004 | Decide TP dashboard integration depth (project tab vs standalone navigation) | Investigation | Dashboard | P1 |\n49\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E005 | Decide AgentRuntime CR cleanup semantics on component removal | Investigation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n50\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E006 | Resolve OTEL trace sink requirement from parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) | Investigation | Kagenti | P0 |\n51\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E007 | Konflux onboarding: kagenti-operator image (FIPS Go build, UBI9) | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n52\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E008 | Konflux onboarding: AuthBridge proxy sidecar image (FIPS Go build, UBI9) | Implementation | Kagenti | P1 |\n53\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E009 | License validation for kagenti midstream repositories | Implementation | Kagenti | P0 |\n54\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E010 | KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator (deploy side: CRD, action pipeline, kustomize manifests, Managed) | Implementation | Platform / ODH Operator | P0 |\n55\t| RHAISTRAT-8006-E011 | OLM/CSV packaging with RELATED_IMAGE entries for disconnected install | Imple