onent\n150\t  controller (E010), CSV packaging (E011), QE (E013), or the CSV branch epic\n151\t  (BRANCH-B-E017). The Konflux-built image digests are configuration\n152\t  references filled in at execution time; the coupling is enforced by acceptance criteria\n153\t  (\"Konflux-built image with SHA256-pinned digest available\") on the consuming epics, never by\n154\t  DAG dependencies. Wiring such edges would serialize work that must run in parallel.\n155\t- No edge between license validation (E009) and Konflux onboarding (E007/E008) — Rule 7/8:\n156\t  parallel start. Rule 9 (license → general implementation serial) has no target here: this\n157\t  strategy contains no general-purpose implementation epic built on the kagenti code (runtime\n158\t  features are out of scope, tracked in RHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589). A license failure would\n159\t  remediate dependency sets inside the Konflux/Dockerfile work, not change epic structure.\n160\t- No repo-onboarding epic: midstream forks already exist per the strategy dependency table.\n161\t\n162\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n163\t\n164\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n165\t| --- | --- | --- |\n166\t| Operator images built via Konflux with FIPS-compliant Go compilation on UBI9 | P0 | E007 |\n167\t| Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR, standard component controller pattern | P0 | E010 (Managed deployment), E019 (Removed transition) |\n168\t| `managementState: Removed` cleans up all operator-managed resources | P0 | E019 (semantics decided by E005) |\n169\t| Upstream-first policy (kagenti/* before opendatahub-io/* midstream) | P0 | E007, E008, E009 (process constraint on all Kagenti midstream work) |\n170\t| Tech Preview maturity, explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC) | P0 | E010 |\n171\t| Dashboard integration infrastructure: BFF plugin + feature flag | P1 | E012 |\n172\t| OLM/CSV packaging with `RELATED_IMAGE_*` for disconnected install | P1 | E011 (+ BRANCH-B-E017 if additional AuthBridge variants are required for TP) |\n173\t| AuthBridge proxy sidecar image via Konflux with FIPS compliance | P1 | E008 (+ BRANCH-B-E015 for additional variants) |\n174\t| Multi-arch builds (AMD64 required; arm64 if free) | P2 | E007, E008 (build-configuration acceptance criteria, not separate epics — incidental to the same build work) |\n175\t\n176\tAll 9 HLRs covered; no orphaned requirements; no epic without HLR (or strategy-AC) trace.\n177\t\n178\tStrategy-level acceptance criteria coverage notes:\n179\t\n180\t- DSC enablement, Removed cleanup, documentation MUSTs → E010, E019 (cleanup semantics from\n181\t  E005), E014.\n182\t- Console/API discovery of agents → E012 (TP read-only agent list).\n183\t- AgentRuntime CR selection/discovery, metadata sync on rollouts, degraded condition (SHOULD),\n184\t  Deployment-deletion garbage collection → upstream operator runtime behavior, explicitly out of\n185\t  scope (RHAIRFE-7587/7588). Not covered by design.\n186\t- Sandbox auto-registration (COULD) → out of scope; see Health Warnings.\n187\t- OTEL trace sink (open MUST from parent RFE) → E006 + BRANCH-B-E016 (wiring) +\n188\t  BRANCH-B-E018 (customer documentation).\n189\t\n190\t## Health Warnings\n191\t\n192\t1. **Open parent-RFE MUST (OTEL trace sink)** — the parent RFE (RHAIRFE-7451) carries an OTEL\n193\t   trace sink MUST not reflected in this strategy's HLRs; under team discussion. Modeled as\n194\t   Investigation E006 with conditional branch epics BRANCH-B-E016 (wiring) and BRANCH-B-E018\n195\t   (customer documentation). If the discussion lands late, TP docs and QE scope shift.\n196\t2. **Dashboard architecture-context discrepancy** — architecture context (odh-dashboard.md,\n197\t   RHOAI 3.6-ea.1) shows an existing `agent-ops` federated BFF module with per-agent RBAC that\n198\t   the strategy does not mention (it cites only 7 plugins / ports 8043-8643). The dashboard epic\n199\t   must reconcile reuse/extension of the existing agent-ops module against building a new kagenti\n200