{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-84d4865572005dd0","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8006-E010\n3\ttitle: KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8006\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform\n6\tteam: Platform / ODH Operator\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8006-E001,RHAISTRAT-8006-E003\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the upstream validation finds functional gaps or an unstable\n16\t    AgentRuntime CRD, the manifest baseline and possibly the controller scope (e.g.,\n17\t    deferred MLflowReconciler / ClientRegistrationController per negotiated TP scope\n18\t    reduction) must be rewritten before the component controller work can proceed.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# KagentiOperator DSC component controller in rhods-operator\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tRegister kagenti-operator as a new standard component in the rhods-operator component\n41\tregistry, following the established 16-component pattern. This delivers the deploy side of the\n42\tDataScienceCluster (DSC) enablement path: a new `KagentiOperator` component CRD, a component\n43\tcontroller implementing the standard action pipeline, kustomize manifest integration from the\n44\tmidstream fork, and the `managementState: Managed` deployment with Tech Preview opt-in\n45\t(defaults to Removed). The `Managed` → `Removed` cleanup transition is a separable sub-deliverable\n46\tcarried by the cleanup-focused epic split out of this workstream (the strategy prices the combined\n47\tcontroller workstream at 2-3 sprints, and cleanup semantics have their own investigation, risk\n48\trow, and NFR).\n49\t\n50\t## Description of upstream dependencies\n51\t\n52\tThis epic is gated on two resolved unknowns: the upstream validation of the kagenti-operator\n53\t(controllers present, CRD stable, baseline manifest commit pinned) and the Keycloak /\n54\tClientRegistrationController TP configuration decision. Each changes what the manifests and\n55\tcontroller must deploy, so the epic starts once they are resolved.\n56\t\n57\t## Scope\n58\t\n59\t- Define the `KagentiOperator` kind in the `components.platform.opendatahub.io/v1alpha1`\n60\t  group, following the pattern of `ModelRegistry`, `Trainer`, and other component CRDs, and\n61\t  extend the DSC CR schema accordingly.\n62\t- Implement the component controller with the standard action pipeline (initialize, releases,\n63\t  kustomize render, deploy, check deployments, garbage collect) and register it in the\n64\t  component registry.\n65\t- Integrate kustomize manifests from the midstream fork at pinned commits (via the standard\n66\t  manifest-fetch script) into the prefetched-manifests layout, with RHOAI-specific overlays for\n67\t  namespace (`redhat-ods-applications`), image references, and RBAC adjustments.\n68\t- Implement `managementState` handling for the deploy side: `Managed` deploys the operator\n69\t  (Deployment, CRDs, RBAC, mutating webhook).\n70\t- Default the component to `Removed` (explicit opt-in) for Tech Preview.\n71\t- Apply the decided TP configuration for the ClientRegistrationController / Keycloak dependency\n72\t  in the manifest overlays.\n73\t- The `Managed` → `Removed` transition — deletion of all operator-managed resources per the\n74\t  decided cleanup contract — is not in this epic's scope; it is carried by the cleanup-focused\n75\t  epic split out of this workstream.\n76\t\n77\t## Acceptance Criteria\n78\t\n79\t- Given a fresh RHOAI deployment with the kagenti component `managementState: Managed`, when\n80\t  the DSC controller reconciles, the kagenti-operator Deployment is created in\n81\t  `redhat-ods-applications` with the Konflux-built image (SHA256-pinned digest available as a\n82\t  configuration reference), measured by a Ready deployment with `app=kagenti-operator`.\n83\t- Component defaults to `Removed` (opt-in); existing clusters are unaffected by upgrade.\n84\t- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n85\t- Manifests are pinned to the validated upstream/midstream baseline commit.\n86\t- The Keycloak / ClientRegistrationController TP configuration decision is resolved and its\n87\t  outcome applied in the manifest overlays before this epic completes (decision gate on the\n88\t  Keycloak runtime-dependency investigation — this epic is blocked on that outcome).\n89\t\n90\t## HLR Traceability\n91\t\n92\t- P0: Operator enabled/disabled via DataScienceCluster CR following the standard component\n93\t  controller pattern (the `Managed` deployment and component state surface; the `Removed`\n94\t  cleanup is carried by the cleanup-focused epic).\n95\t- P0: Tech Preview maturity with explicit opt-in (disabled by default in DSC).\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-be364346b92c0a7e","agent_id":"a96bcd1a69cb8e30f","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"e1bd8d4a-7e1b-4a3b-8c0d-8f0fc1d992a5","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:09:57.509Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84d4865572005dd0","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Second revise RHAISTRAT-8006"}
