 decision), their own risk row (orphaned resources on\n46\tcomponent disable), and their own NFR (resource cleanup on disable).\n47\t\n48\t## Description of upstream dependencies\n49\t\n50\tThis epic is gated on the cleanup-semantics decision: whether component removal includes\n51\tcross-namespace AgentRuntime CRD deletion (destroying user-created CRs) or leaves them in place\n52\tdefines the garbage-collection contract this epic implements. It also builds on the component\n53\tcontroller, `KagentiOperator` CRD, and registry registration delivered by the deploy-side\n54\tcontroller work — the Removed transition is implemented in that controller.\n55\t\n56\t## Scope\n57\t\n58\t- Implement the `Managed` → `Removed` transition in the component controller: delete the\n59\t  controller Deployment, ClusterRoles/ClusterRoleBindings/Roles/RoleBindings, the AgentRuntime\n60\t  CRD, the mutating webhook configuration, and namespace-scoped resources (ConfigMaps, Secrets)\n61\t  in `redhat-ods-applications`, per the decided cleanup contract.\n62\t- Implement the decided cross-namespace AgentRuntime CR handling (cluster-wide CRD deletion\n63\t  versus leaving user-created CRs in place), including a finalizer-based enumeration of owned\n64\t  resources where the decided contract requires it (strategy risk: DSC component cleanup leaves\n65\t  orphaned resources).\n66\t- Apply the decided cleanup contract's resource list, namespace scope, and ordering exactly, so\n67\t  the QE lifecycle validation can test it with resources in multiple namespaces.\n68\t\n69\t## Acceptance Criteria\n70\t\n71\t- Given the kagenti component changed from `Managed` to `Removed`, when the component controller\n72\t  reconciles the state change, all operator-managed resources (Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook\n73\t  configuration) are deleted per the decided cleanup contract, verified for resources in multiple\n74\t  namespaces, measured by `kubectl get deployment -n redhat-ods-applications -l app=kagenti-operator`\n75\t  returning no results and the AgentRuntime CRD returning not found.\n76\t- The AgentRuntime CR cleanup-semantics decision is resolved and the garbage-collection logic\n77\t  implements the decided cleanup contract before this epic completes (decision gate on the\n78\t  cleanup-semantics investigation — this epic is blocked on that outcome).\n79\t- Build pipeline green for rhods-operator changes (Konflux).\n80\t\n81\t## HLR Traceability\n82\t\n83\t- P0: When disabled (`managementState: Removed`), all operator-managed resources are cleaned up:\n84\t  controller Deployment, RBAC, CRDs, webhook configuration, namespace-scoped resources.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a28eb7d292fbf1b3","agent_id":"adbb7fab2ae44893a","session_id":"ec1d2a2a-7323-4c5d-bb4c-fc6cac99ed4f","uuid":"c31667f3-2447-4525-a50c-71eeaf5c1d3e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T10:10:09.018Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b5bab136d0746b8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Final re-review RHAISTRAT-8006"}
