oach` addresses only the Keycloak (E003) dimension of its two\ngates; the E001 image-contract/CRD-baseline dimension is gated only via the epic's ACs rather\nthan the frontmatter fallback.\n\n### 5. AI Implementability Scoring (1/2)\nSignal-set typing is correct everywhere: all 13 Implementation epics (including branch epics)\ncarry `ai_signals` (9-signal rubric); all 6 Investigations carry `investigation_signals`\n(5-signal rubric); all 19 rationale files exist and their values match frontmatter. Most values\nare well-justified: E002/E004/E006 correctly score source_accessibility 0 / human_judgment -2\nfor decision-type questions; E001/E003 correctly score +1 for source-determinable questions;\nE007/E008/E010/E012 negative human_process_gates match the pending Konflux/Architecture/UXD\ngates; BRANCH-B-E016's negative signals match the unspecified OTEL scope. One arguable value:\nE005's `source_accessibility: 1` — the gating question (cross-namespace cleanup semantics for\nuser-created CRs) is a design/product decision whose answer does not exist in any readable\nrecord; the readable rhods-operator GC patterns inform but do not determine it, so the rubric's\n0-condition (\"decision still under review\") arguably applies. Borderline, not a contradiction.\n\n### 6. Acceptance Criteria Quality (2/2)\nEvery epic has testable ACs derived from the strategy (the Given/when/then ACs for DSC\ndeployment, Removed cleanup, disconnected install, and dashboard list are carried over\nfaithfully; the strategy's `agentrimes` CRD-name typo is silently normalized in E019's AC).\nRule-mandated ACs verified across all qualifying epics: Rule 24 technically-reviewed ACs on both\ndocs-authoring epics (E014, BRANCH-B-E018); Rule 25 build-pipeline-green ACs on E010, E011,\nE012, E019 plus check-payload/green-build ACs on all three Konflux epics (E007, E008,\nBRANCH-B-E015) and BRANCH-B-E016/E017; Rule 23 n/a (new component, not a replacement — E012\nnonetheless carries the feature-flag hiding AC). No bare draft-ID references (E0xx) in any epic\nbody — cross-epic references use descriptive phrasing; only frontmatter uses full epic IDs.\n\n### 7. Completeness (2/2)\nAll in-scope strategy items are covered: Konflux builds (E007/E008), component controller\n(E010), Removed cleanup (E019), CSV packaging (E011), dashboard integration (E012), license\nvalidation (E009), QE (E013), docs (E014). The out-of-scope boundary (runtime behavior →\nRHAIRFE-7587/7588/7589, identity → RHAIRFE-7408) is respected and documented rather than\nsilently dropped. All five strategy open questions plus the parent-RFE OTEL MUST are accounted\nfor: four become Investigations E001–E005, the OTEL question becomes E006 with conditional\nbranch E016/E018, and the minimal-image-contract question is carried as a finalized-contract AC\non E014 with a transparent justification (owned by RHAIRFE-7588; no epic's existence or approach\nchanges on the answer) in health warning #4. Strategy-level context is carried forward: the\nwebhook-ordering and port-collision risks appear in E013/E012 scopes and ACs, the Konflux\nlead-time risk drives the root placement of E007/E008, and the architecture-context\ndiscrepancy (existing agent-ops BFF module, ten BFFs vs the strategy's cited seven) is flagged\nas health warning #2 and addressed in E012's scope (reconcile before building new). Conditional\nbranches cover both bounded outcomes of E002 and E006. Docs-authoring epic present (Documentation\nSupport gate is \"pending human review\" rather than \"Yes\", but the strategy's MUST AC and\nimpacted-teams table require installation docs, and E014 covers them). The RFE MUST \"see what\neach agent can do (skills, protocols, endpoints)\" is only partially covered by the TP read-only\nlist view — this limitation is the strategy's own TP scoping (\"basic agent visibility... full\nagent management UI is out of scope\"), which the decomposition carries rather than invents, and\nit is noted in the coverage note